            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="HAU01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Moses</forename>
                        <surname>Haughton</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1772">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1848"/>
                    <occupation>miniaturist and painter</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Nephew of Moses Haughton, the elder (1734-1804) Haughton was a friend of
                            Fuseli, whose work he engraved and with whom he may have lived in
                            Somserset House. Fuseli's widow lived with Moses Haughton after Fuseli's
                            death. There is an issue about whether Houghton entries ought to be
                            coded for Haughton, since they appear shortly before the acquaintance
                            develops (January and February 1809), and Godwin does not always
                            identify names correctly on first meeting. Moreover, both events are at
                            Johnson's with Fuseli. We have, accordingly, coded Houghton for
                            Haughton. The entries after 1814 we believe are to Graves Haugton,
                            although we cannot be sure this iss sso, especially for the 827 entry.
                            The 1833 entry is unequivocal because of Grave Haughton's role in the
                            Asiatic Society that Godwin refers to. See ODNB</p>
                    </note>
